<p>Cuban prosecutors have charged six people with terrorism after a US-flagged speedboat carrying weapons was involved in a deadly shootout with Cuba’s coast guard on Feb. 25. Cuban authorities say the group came from the United States intending to sow chaos and attack military units, and they have displayed weapons they say they recovered from the vessel. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said the episode was not a US operation, while some US politicians have questioned Cuba’s account and called for an independent investigation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GqVPwJR-7i8gQF5F99HgPUuPmA_ZAW5N42CenG9PVMcSgfxm2EsK6nuQykvC7N8SofDKO-p-xH22FryyknBEEXB1rBp2zT-WtTv0kv_v7tSIM_JnNZibta_OavTUaFKAkgSc71Rea0efloxpuMvYMnterFrt2qiAx4xw3k2cJa5Y16bqJQCRU-IxDFEDBy7aIdKvo0o__RmrOTLtmujtdffc_pB78peUh7v8LuBYAm_-ySHxBm7NNd6oXviZYG6ustfEvcfb-wwk5nanow' alt='Weapons that Cuban authorities say were recovered from a speedboat in Cuban waters are displayed during a media presentation in Havana, Feb. 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Casualties reported: Cuban officials said four people on board the speedboat were killed after the coast guard opened fire during the confrontation.</li><li>Weapons displayed: Cuban authorities said the boat carried firearms of various calibers — including 14 rifles and 11 pistols — along with nearly 13,000 rounds of ammunition.</li><li>Nearshore incident: Cuban officials said the speedboat came within about one nautical mile of Cuba’s shores during the Feb. 25 shootout.</li><li>Who fired first (Cuba’s account): Cuba’s Interior Ministry said the exiles on the speedboat opened fire on a border guard vessel.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuban government (Interior Ministry/prosecutors): Authorities say the US-registered boat brought weapons from the United States to destabilize Cuba, and that those aboard opened fire on a border guard vessel; prosecutors have filed terrorism charges against six detainees. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-charges-6-with-terrorism-over-speedboat-shootout/a-76207233'>DW</a>)</li><li>US State Department: Secretary of State Marco Rubio said the incident was not a US operation. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-charges-6-with-terrorism-over-speedboat-shootout/a-76207233'>DW</a>)</li><li>US politicians (skeptics): Some US politicians said they doubt Cuba’s version of events and called for an independent investigation. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-cuba-speedboat-soldier-terrorism/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-charges-6-with-terrorism-over-speedboat-shootout/a-76207233'>Cuba charges 6 with terrorism over speedboat shootout</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/cuba-charges-six-exiles-terrorism-speedboat-attack'>Cuba charges six exiles with terrorism in wake of deadly speedboat attack</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-cuba-speedboat-soldier-terrorism/'>Cuba charges six exiles with terrorism for firing on soldiers from speedboat</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/cuba-charges-six-exiles-with-terrorism-in-speedboat-attack'>Cuba charges six exiles with terrorism in speedboat attack</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/04/cuba-charges-six-with-terrorism-in-us-speedboat-shootout_6751074_4.html'>Cuba charges six with terrorism in US speedboat shootout</a> - lemonde.fr</li></ul>